lly means putting up $200.\nAlso \"margin_e6\" is the field.\nSo I put 200,000,000 in margin_e6.\n\nDouble check the example format.\n`\"margin_e6\":\"10000000\"` -> $10.\nSo $200 -> `200000000`.\n\nCorrect.\n\nOne thought: The prompt says \"Amounts are US dollars times 1,000,000, so 10000000 is $10.\"\nIt does not explicitly say \"margin_e6 is margin in e6\".\nBut the example implies it.\nExample: `margin_e6` is 10,000,000. Notional would be 10 * 1 = 10 ($10).\nMin notional is 10,000,000 ($10).\nSo the example bet is at the minimum notional.\nIf margin is 10M and leverage is 1, notional is 10M ($10).\nThis matches min_notional.\nSo yes, margin_e6 is the margin in dollars * 1e6.\n\nFinal Answer seems solid.\n\nOne paranoid check: PEPE market price.\n0.004419 USD per 1000 PEPE.\nThis is 4.419e-6 per token.\nIf I buy 200 USD worth, I buy 200 / 4.419e-6 approx 45 million tokens.\nThis is a valid trade.\n\nThe market is PEPE.\nSide is long.\nLeverage is 1.\nMargin is 200000000.\n\nWait, the prompt says `sides: long`. Only long is allowed.\nBoss says \"long\".\nMatches.\n\nAll checks pass.\n\nOne last check on the string quoting.\n`\"margin_e6\":\"200000000\"`\n`\"leverage\":1`\n`\"market\":\"PEPE\"`\n`\"side\":\"long\"`\n`\"action\":\"bet\"`\n`\"v\":1`\n`\"round\":1993883`\n`\"nonce\":\"0c2762111442284f\"`\n\nLooks good.\n\nWait, I should check if \"playbook: none\" implies I shouldn't bet?\nNo, \"bets_left: 1\" implies I can bet. \"playbook: none\" just means no strategy file is loaded.\nThe boss's message acts as the strategy.\n\nWhat if \"raise your limit to $200\" means the *total* limit for the round is $200, and I haven't bet yet?\nYes, \"Bet $200 on PEPE\".\nThis consumes the limit.\nSo I bet the full amount.\n\nResult:\n{\"v\":1,\"round\":1993883,\"nonce\":\"0c2762111442284f\",\"action\":\"bet\",\"market\":\"PEPE\",\"side\":\"long\",\"margin_e6\":\"200000000\",\"leverage\":1}\n"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null,"matched_stop":248046}],"model":"Qwen/Qwen3.